<urn:atm:triage:finding/AO27-HARNESS-F001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AO27-HARNESS-F001" ;
  triage:title "M5AttemptLedger contract implemented but never called" ;
  triage:description "The M5AttemptLedger safety contract (SuiteIntent, CompleteSuiteAttempt, derive_accepted_m5, crash-safe append-before-execute) is fully implemented in scripts/smoke/benchmark_suite.py but is never instantiated or called outside its own unit test. The actual entry points (run_admission_capacity.py and benchmark_report.py) derive PASS/FAIL from each target's latest evidence file independently, bypassing the ledger's restore-verified check, intent/completion pairing, 3-consecutive-attempt requirement, and candidate-lineage check. This means the PR ships the ledger's building blocks but not the actual AO2.7 safety and acceptance deliverable." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ao2" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "HARNESS" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "deferred" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-22T21:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Fixing as originally scoped (wiring M5AttemptLedger into current entry points) is throwaway: AO2.10 (docs/plans/phase-ao2/sprint-AO2-10-benchmark-data-contract.md) replaces this PASS/FAIL derivation path with a single-owner classify_status() model and deletes the unused ledger module outright (AO2.10 deliverable 8) rather than wiring it in. AO2.10/AO2.11 are infrastructure sprints (v4 schema/runner emission, then rendering) and do not themselves restore an equivalent acceptance safety net. Re-promoted 2026-08-24 from 'pending AO2.10' to 'pending AO2.12/AO2.13': neither sprint doc currently names a replacement for the deleted 3-consecutive-attempt/crash-safe acceptance discipline, so this finding stays open and must be explicitly re-evaluated once AO2.10+AO2.11 land -- either as an AO2.13 (canonical benchmark-run workflow, docs/plans/phase-ao2/sprint-AO2-13-benchmark-run-skill.md) deliverable addition enforcing an equivalent safety gate, or closed with an explicit team-lead/quality-mgr rationale for why no replacement is required. 2026-08-25/26 re-evaluation (fenix, acting under Rand's 'make any calls on my behalf' delegation; quality-mgr independent review; both flagged for Rand's ratification on return): of the ledger's four original guarantees, restore-verified (durability_after_restart, expected-vs-observed post-restart mailbox count) and candidate-lineage (per-attempt binary_hashes, SHA256 of atm/atm-daemon) are covered by the shipped AO2.10-AO2.13 contract as-is -- quality-mgr confirmed both present in real m5-atmbench campaign JSON. The remaining two guarantees -- crash-safe intent/completion pairing, and the 3-consecutive-clean-run acceptance bar for a baseline change -- are NOT replaced by any shipped code, and quality-mgr found live evidence of both gaps during the tcp/tls floor review on the same date: an AO2.15 launchd trigger attempt that never reached measurement left no artifact at all until arch-ctm manually reported it (the crash-visibility gap), and the floor revision under review at that point relied on only 2 real runs, not 3 clean ones (the acceptance-bar gap). Per Rand's standing benchmark-infra freeze ('behavioral rules over machinery'), no new ledger component is being built. Instead, commit 73e243fec (docs(benchmark): retain official trigger attempts, on feature/ao2-15-benchmark-official-trigger) amends .claude/skills/benchmark-run/SKILL.md and the AO2.15 sprint doc with two behavioral rules quality-mgr independently verified: (1) every `just benchmark-official` invocation must leave a committed, pushed artifact -- a campaign JSON when measurement completes, or a timestamped failed-attempt note under docs/plans/phase-ao2/evidence/ when it cannot reach measurement -- and the AO2.15 launchd non-start already has its retroactive note (AO2-15-launchd-trigger-nonstart-20260826.md, includes trigger, branch/SHA, failure boundary, and cleanup proof); (2) any future baselines.json floor change requires >= 3 clean, published official runs for the same host/target/contract, with failed or partial attempts explicitly excluded from the count, and existing campaign snapshots remain immutable under a later revision. quality-mgr additionally confirmed the just-approved revision 4 (tcp/tls floors) in fact has 3 real runs (20260825T045840Z, 20260826T001441Z, 20260826T002410Z) all clearing the new floors, satisfying rule (2) retroactively as well as being grandfathered by Rand's direct D3 sign-off. Disposition: guarantees 1+4 covered by the shipped contract; guarantees 2+3 replaced by the above behavioral rules rather than new machinery per the infra freeze; this finding stays 'deferred' (not closed) pending Rand's ratification of this framing on return -- flip to closed on ratification, or reopens as scoped work if he wants the ledger component back instead." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AO2.7 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-22T21:09:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AO27-HARNESS-F001/ao2-7-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AO27-HARNESS-F001/ao2-7-2> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "3" .

